cff-version: 1.2.0
title: A 90% ECG threshold does not hold at another hospital or in another care setting
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abbou
    given-names: Ruben
repository-code: https://github.com/rabbou/ecg-conformal-shift
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Measures what a decision threshold set for 90% on one population delivers
  within each label once it is carried unchanged to another. Infarction
  thresholds fitted on PTB-XL are carried to hospitals in Shandong and
  Chongqing, and five corpora take the calibrating role in turn on five other
  diagnoses. Structural heart disease thresholds fitted on Columbia inpatients
  in EchoNext are carried to its outpatients, for four models. A single tuned
  threshold, pooled conformal calibration and per-label conformal calibration
  are compared, with what each defers, what the AUROC and the deferral rate
  show without labels, and how many local labels repair the transfer.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - electrocardiography
  - structural heart disease
  - myocardial infarction
  - distribution shift
  - class-conditional coverage
